# SERVE behind Caddy — one domain, automatic HTTPS (Let's Encrypt).
#
# Replace YOUR_DOMAIN with the real domain (its DNS A/AAAA record must point
# at this server, ports 80 and 443 open). The backend serves everything:
# /, /staff/, /admin/, /api and /socket.io (WEB_ROOT set, see
# docs/deployment.md), so Caddy only terminates TLS and forwards. Caddy passes
# WebSocket upgrades and X-Forwarded-* headers through by default; run the
# backend with TRUST_PROXY=1.

YOUR_DOMAIN {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5001
}
